ing it is that you  have this anti-hero right and it's this  tragic ending for them they get caught  they're literally lying on the ground  it's like the identical shot of walter  white at the end and what's also  frustrating why it doesn't work though  doing that is because harrison's kind of  taking the role here of jesse pinkman  and the difference between that of them  riding off into the sunset right  is that  jessie pinkman you loved jesse pinkman  you know i don't love harrison i don't  like harrison so  i'm not gonna sit there and feel  connected when he's having his moment at  the end here and happy for him and  that's the problem here is that harrison  hasn't played as that character during  the whole season that we're supposed to  really like and that we're like oh so  attached to harrison you know we're  attached to dexter and  they didn't do a good enough job then if  they're gonna end it this way with  harrison kind of being the one we're  supposed to attach to and feel for a lot  you know that had to be work done early  on and i don't think that was done  enough and i think that's  problematic because the actor is so good  but he's not  the type of character you really see is  likable you're not like he's not someone  you're like yeah i'm behind harrison  i hope to god they're not planning to do  like an el camino spin-off like breaking  bad day with jessie with harrison  because i will not watch and you know  it's interesting from a business  standpoint with showtime that you know  he killed dexter this show is doing  great dexter new blood ratings wise  review wise fans loved it until maybe  this episode but i i don't know what  they're gonna do now because  business-wise yeah you would say  bring another season but you killed  dexter so if you're saying we're gonna  lead into harrison's life now  i would not watch that and even if they  said okay if we want to get michael c  hall back to get people to actually  watch his thing and bring him in maybe  the deb harry roll i still wouldn't  watch that that's not enough for me i'm  not i'm not what harrison is not a  character i want to watch a full show  about i don't like him enough i don't  care about him enough and the other  thing is that what the season did was  you know harrison was the only day of  big red herring and that you know dexter  was wrong about him that he doesn't  really have dexter's exact  violent urges like to the extremes that  dexter does and he doesn't really have a  dark passenger per se it's just anger  like he's talking about so  in that sense that i thought was earned  i thought they did a good job of kind of  misdirecting you there and what was  weird to me and a lot of people were  talking about too is this moment which  is big with dexter and logan and  it did still feel forced in how he  killed logan because they knew they  needed that to have a reason for  harrison to kill dexter and i wish  that maybe harrison's  choice to want to kill dexter and turn  him in  wasn't so just made at the end there and  that was flipped so fast like i wish  that was kind of something that was more  earned and he connects maybe things that  went on the whole season that would make  him want to do that than just something  that just recently happened in that  moment  so  it's frustrating and  i also think i didn't mention much of my  review in the past but it's a good point  about the plot hole people have made  about the ketamine and it being m99 that  he originally used in the series as the  bay harbor butcher and that had that was  a big writing mess up  which it was but i didn't take it as  something that it was like the biggest  deal because it was part of the way  angela found out who dexter was and that  could be frustrating but i was shocked  that they almost highlighted their error  in this finale um because her saying the  big line that about tell me about  ketamine now it feels like okay this is  ridiculous you can't have this big of a  writing error and then highlight it and  make me go along with this that is where  it gets too much now it's like okay come  on this that's like amateur hour stuff  and that really is just shocking that  not even someone like michael c hall  would just bring up like you know why  don't we just have him  like even address it and talk about it  maybe it was originally m990 switch  something had to be put in there  anywhere any scene the whole season and  that would have worked better so  that was strange and  i think what's tough is that  this whole season was you know mostly  really good and like i've been saying  it's been like firing on all cylinders  the past couple episodes i think the  letdown part of it  is that you know it kind of just  felt like it didn't have everything tied  together perfectly from what was  happening in the season  um it feels like all the curt stuff  became a distant afterthought we have no  idea what the deal was with the  billionaire if he was just a red herring  that's his only purpose i still think i  don't like when that's written like that  i think that just having character serve  the plot again is always just  not great writing and frustrating you  always want it to come out of character  the whole way through and how it really  serves dexter not the plot you know and  that's my other frustration is that  what is the show trying to say here if  it's almost saying that harrison is  better off with his father dead but  again taking that route  is going against the person we're  connected to in the show i want the  ending to connect to something about  dexter and i don't like that i don't  like that  if we think of the whole timeline of the  show it's like  to me it felt like i was saying yeah  maybe this guy's just better off dead  you know i don't think that's smart  ending in my opinion and that might just  be personal preference but  i wasn't crazy about that either now i  don't think this was all bad i think you  know it's the fi